0/08/20230720_Kim_HyunA_in_July_2023_01_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20230720_Kim_HyunA_in_July_2023_01_(cropped).png","author":"K-POPIT 케이팝잇","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"bio":{"text":"Kim Hyun-ah, known professionally as Hyuna (stylized as HyunA), is a South Korean singer-songwriter, rapper and model. She debuted as a member of the girl group Wonder Girls in February 2007. Upon leaving the ensemble shortly after, Hyuna subsequently left JYP Entertainment and joined the girl group 4Minute. The group debuted in June 2009 under Cube Entertainment. In 2010, Hyuna began a solo career with a style she described as \"performance-oriented music\". Her solo debut single \"Change\" charted at number-two on South Korea's Gaon Digital Chart. In 2011, Hyuna gained wider public recognition with the release of her first extended play Bubble Pop!.","title":"Hyuna","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyuna"}},"Q240082":{"id":"Q240082","name":"Seo Joo-hyun","ko":"서현","birthName":"서주현","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Seo Ju-hyun","Seohyun"],"birth":"1991-06-28","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor","film actor","model","stage actor","composer"],"debut":"2007","agencies":[{"name":"SM Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483938","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q20153","name":"Girls' Generation","start":"2007","end":""},{"id":"Q484588","name":"Girls' Generation-TTS","start":"2012","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/seojuhyun_s/","x":"https://x.com/sjhsjh0628","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCcbVxBwXT6MATv14d9dfjVA","spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/artist/5uM1Et50auro2hTS6ZLcmT","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/4c76ba5a-281b-4785-b99f-0c0146f1bac3"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/75/Seohyun_at_Incheon_International_Airport_in_February_2019_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seohyun_at_Incheon_International_Airport_in_February_2019_(1).jpg","author":"SparkleS805","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"bio":{"text":"Seo Ju-hyun, known professionally as Seohyun, is a South Korean singer, actress, and songwriter. She debuted as a member of girl group Girls' Generation (and later its subgroup Girls' Generation-TTS) in August 2007, which went on to become one of the best-selling artists in South Korea and one of South Korea's most widely known girl groups worldwide. Seohyun released her first extended play Don't Say No in 2017. She left SM Entertainment later that year, although she remains as a member of Girls' Generation. Aside from her music career, she has established herself as an actress.","title":"Seohyun","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seohyun"},"positions":["Lead vocalist"],"mbti":"ENTJ","factSources":{"positions":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%84%9C%ED%98%84%28%EC%86%8C%EB%85%80%EC%8B%9C%EB%8C%80%29"},"mbti":{"name":"Namu Wiki (2021 dump)","license":"CC BY-NC-SA 2.0 KR","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.0/kr/","base":"https://namu.wiki/w/","url":"https://namu.wiki/w/%EC%84%9C%ED%98%84%28%EC%86%8C%EB%85%80%EC%8B%9C%EB%8C%80%29"}}},"Q24832146":{"id":"Q24832146","name":"Lim Na-young","ko":"임나영","birthName":"임나영","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Lim Na Young","Lim Nayoung","Im Na-young","Im Na Young","Im Nayoung","Nayoung"],"birth":"1995-12-18","death":"","birthplace":"Seoul","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2016","agencies":[{"name":"Pledis Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q45282","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q26265886","name":"Pri